    {
      "id": "exam/edexcel-9ma0-02-2021-october/q8",
      "question": "<p>The curve <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"C\"></span> has equation</p><div class=\"equation\" data-math=\"px^3+qxy+3y^2=26\" data-display=\"true\"></div><p>where <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"p\"></span> and <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"q\"></span> are constants.</p><ol class=\"parts\"><li>Show that<div class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\\frac{\\mathrm dy}{\\mathrm dx}=\\frac{apx^2+bqy}{qx+cy}\" data-display=\"true\"></div>where <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"a\"></span>, <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"b\"></span> and <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"c\"></span> are integers to be found. <span class=\"marks\">(4)</span></li></ol><p>Given that</p><ul><li>the point <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"P(-1,-4)\"></span> lies on <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"C\"></span></li><li>the normal to <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"C\"></span> at <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"P\"></span> has equation <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"19x+26y+123=0\"></span></li></ul><ol class=\"parts\" start=\"2\"><li>find the value of <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"p\"></span> and the value of <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"q\"></span>. <span class=\"marks\">(5)</span></li></ol>",
