    {
      "id": "exam/edexcel-9ma0-02-2021-october/q10",
      "question": "<p>The time, <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"T\"></span> seconds, that a pendulum takes to complete one swing is modelled by the formula</p><div class=\"equation\" data-math=\"T=al^b\" data-display=\"true\"></div><p>where <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"l\"></span> metres is the length of the pendulum and <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"a\"></span> and <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"b\"></span> are constants.</p><ol class=\"parts\"><li>Show that this relationship can be written in the form<div class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\\log_{10}T=b\\log_{10}l+\\log_{10}a\" data-display=\"true\"></div><span class=\"marks\">(2)</span></li></ol><figure class=\"practice-figure\" style=\"max-width:70mm;margin:2mm auto\"><img src=\"resources/exams/edexcel-9ma0-02-2021-october/q10-figure.svg\" alt=\"Figure 3: a straight line graph of log10 T against log10 l, passing through (-0.7, 0) on the horizontal axis and ending at (0.21, 0.45), crossing the vertical axis above O.\"></figure><p>A student carried out an experiment to find the values of the constants <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"a\"></span> and <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"b\"></span>.</p><p>The student recorded the value of <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"T\"></span> for different values of <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"l\"></span>.</p><p>Figure 3 shows the linear relationship between <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\log_{10}l\"></span> and <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\log_{10}T\"></span> for the student’s data.<br>The straight line passes through the points <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"(-0.7, 0)\"></span> and <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"(0.21, 0.45)\"></span></p><p>Using this information,</p><ol class=\"parts\" start=\"2\"><li>find a complete equation for the model in the form<div class=\"equation\" data-math=\"T=al^b\" data-display=\"true\"></div>giving the value of <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"a\"></span> and the value of <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"b\"></span>, each to 3 significant figures. <span class=\"marks\">(3)</span></li><li>With reference to the model, interpret the value of the constant <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"a\"></span>. <span class=\"marks\">(1)</span></li></ol>",
