      "question": "<figure class=\"practice-figure\" style=\"max-width:60mm;margin:2mm auto\"><img src=\"resources/exams/edexcel-9ma0-02-2021-october/q11-figure.svg\" alt=\"Figure 4: the V-shaped graph y = |2x - 3k| with its vertex on the positive x-axis, the left branch crossing the positive y-axis.\"></figure><p>Figure 4 shows a sketch of the graph with equation</p><div class=\"equation\" data-math=\"y=\\left|2x-3k\\right|\" data-display=\"true\"></div><p>where <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"k\"></span> is a positive constant.</p><ol class=\"parts\"><li>Sketch the graph with equation <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"y=\\mathrm f(x)\"></span> where<div class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\\mathrm f(x)=k-\\left|2x-3k\\right|\" data-display=\"true\"></div>stating<ul><li>the coordinates of the maximum point</li><li>the coordinates of any points where the graph cuts the coordinate axes</li></ul><span class=\"marks\">(4)</span></li><li>Find, in terms of <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"k\"></span>, the set of values of <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"x\"></span> for which<div class=\"equation\" data-math=\"k-\\left|2x-3k\\right|&gt;x-k\" data-display=\"true\"></div>giving your answer in set notation. <span class=\"marks\">(4)</span></li><li>Find, in terms of <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"k\"></span>, the coordinates of the minimum point of the graph with equation<div class=\"equation\" data-math=\"y=3-5\\mathrm f\\left(\\frac12 x\\right)\" data-display=\"true\"></div><span class=\"marks\">(2)</span></li></ol>",
