      "id": "exam/edexcel-9ma0-02-2021-october/q14",
      "question": "<figure class=\"practice-figure\" style=\"max-width:75mm;margin:2mm auto\"><img src=\"resources/exams/edexcel-9ma0-02-2021-october/q14-figure.svg\" alt=\"Figure 5: a cuboid tank with base 8 m by 3 m and height 5 m, containing water to depth h m (shaded), with a tap at the point T at the bottom front corner.\"></figure><p>Water flows at a constant rate into a large tank.</p><p>The tank is a cuboid, with all sides of negligible thickness.</p><p>The base of the tank measures <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"8\\,\\mathrm m\"></span> by <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"3\\,\\mathrm m\"></span> and the height of the tank is <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"5\\,\\mathrm m\"></span>.</p><p>There is a tap at a point <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"T\"></span> at the bottom of the tank, as shown in Figure 5.</p><p>At time <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"t\"></span> minutes after the tap has been opened</p><ul><li>the depth of water in the tank is <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"h\"></span> metres</li><li>water is flowing into the tank at a constant rate of <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"0.48\\,\\mathrm m^3\"></span> per minute</li><li>water is modelled as leaving the tank through the tap at a rate of <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"0.1h\\,\\mathrm m^3\"></span> per minute</li></ul><ol class=\"parts\"><li>Show that, according to the model,<div class=\"equation\" data-math=\"1200\\frac{\\mathrm dh}{\\mathrm dt}=24-5h\" data-display=\"true\"></div><span class=\"marks\">(4)</span></li></ol><p>Given that when the tap was opened, the depth of water in the tank was <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"2\\,\\mathrm m\"></span>,</p><ol class=\"parts\" start=\"2\"><li>show that, according to the model,<div class=\"equation\" data-math=\"h=A+B\\mathrm e^{-kt}\" data-display=\"true\"></div>where <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"A\"></span>, <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"B\"></span> and <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"k\"></span> are constants to be found. <span class=\"marks\">(6)</span></li></ol><p>Given that the tap remains open,</p><ol class=\"parts\" start=\"3\"><li>determine, according to the model, whether the tank will ever become full, giving a reason for your answer. <span class=\"marks\">(2)</span></li></ol>",
